  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Diagnostic Medical Sonography - B.S.', General and Vascular concentration (School of Allied Health Professions, Department of Radiation Technology). 27-month curriculum (9 quarters) leading to eligibility for the ARDMS RVT and RDMS board examinations. The catalog publishes the curriculum split by 9 quarters; quarter sums verified: 14, 13, 13, 15, 16, 14, 15, 12, 15 = 127 = catalog Total Units 127. Each clinical affiliation quarter uses a distinct course number (RTMS 371, 372, 373, 471, 472, 473, 474, 475), so no course repeats. Per-course prerequisites stated in the catalog: RTMS 372 requires RTMS 371; RTMS 373 requires RTMS 372. The remaining published quarter order is the official sequence, so other prereq arrays are intentionally empty. RTCH 492 (Portfolio II) fulfills the service learning requirement per catalog footnote. All students must pass the ARDMS Sonography Principles and Instrumentation (SPI) exam while enrolled. Prerequisites (65 quarter / 44 semester units including the published GE domains; 3.0 GPA; information session; interview) are documented here and not placed in any term.",
